<h2>Appraisal on Port Arthur Hurricane and Wind Claims</h2>
<p>Appraisal comes up often in Jefferson County because so many claims involve large wind losses with disputed scope. Common examples include whole-roof replacement versus repairs to individual slopes, the extent of interior water damage from wind-driven rain, and whether TDI windstorm installation requirements and city permits were priced. Homes with separate TWIA and homeowners policies may face two different appraisal processes, each governed by its own policy or statute. TWIA’s rules allow disputes over the amount of loss to go to appraisal under specific procedures and deadlines; review the policy and <a href="https://www.twia.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">twia.org</a> before invoking it, and see our <a href="/services/twia-windstorm-claims/">TWIA windstorm claims</a> page.</p>

